ill  not succeed other things will go much  faster than anybody had anticipated we  seed for instance now in sustainable  energy generation etc but in combination  with the Green Deal as a roadmap and  extra security provided by things such  as the climate law this will put us on  the right track to achieve climate  neutrality by 2050 and to achieve a  substantial reduction of emissions by  2030 which I hope will be in line with  what the expectations are of the  European Parliament and if properly  assessed for impact can also be  supported by the European Commission  thank you so much for being here today  I will not prolong your agony any longer  by keeping keeping on speaking I count  on your contribution I count on your  solidarity you can count on mine my team  led by the example is at your disposal  if there are things you see that aren't  going well it's nice if you tell us that  things are going well but it's better  you tell us that things are where things  are not going well so that perhaps we  can have an opportunity to fix it this  will continue to be a cooperative factor  we are not just refocusing our economy  shifting it away from carbon to a carbon  neutral we  also reinventing governance we are  reinventing governance because it will  be it will be inclusive governance if it  is to succeed and for that we need all  of you thank you very much  [Applause]
 

